/-!
# Injectivity of Vélu's abscissa map on ψ₂²-roots

Theorem statement: `WeierstrassCurve.veluX_oddOrderSummingSet_injOn_psi2Sq_roots`
(`6ba267b8-a569-5f57-af9f-1e5f8168114c`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `7edf4b36-3fd3-5e7a-b6e2-b672530d51c8`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $L$ be a field in which $2 \neq 0$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $L$ that is
elliptic. Let $n$ be a natural number and let $Q$ be a point of the associated affine curve $W$
whose additive order is exactly $2n+1$. Put $S = \{\,(k \bullet Q).\text{coordsOrZero} : 1 \le k \le
n\,\}$, the image in $L \times L$ of the interval $[1,n]$ under the map sending $k$ to the affine
coordinates of $k \bullet Q$ (the point at infinity being sent to $(0,0)$), and let $X_S(x) = x +
\sum_{P \in S} \bigl( t_P/(x - P_1) + u_P/(x - P_1)^2 \bigr)$ be Vélu's abscissa function `veluX`,
where $t_P = 2 G_x(P) - a_1 G_y(P)$ and $u_P = G_y(P)^2$ in the notation of the project's Vélu data.
Assume $r, r' \in L$ are both roots of the polynomial $\Psi_2^2$ of $W$ (the square of the second
division polynomial, $4x^3 + b_2 x^2 + 2b_4 x + b_6$), and that $X_S(r) = X_S(r')$. The conclusion
is $r = r'$.

This is the injectivity of Vélu's $x$-coordinate map, restricted to the abscissae of the $2$-torsion
of $W$, for the Vélu summing set of a cyclic subgroup of odd order $2n+1$ generated by $Q$. It is
used to show that the Vélu quotient of $W$ by such a subgroup has non-vanishing discriminant, i.e.
that the quotient Weierstrass equation again defines an elliptic curve.

## Explanation of the source proof

